abstract: "NEUROSCAN is an enterprise-grade clinical neuro-radiology platform and academic benchmarking suite for autonomous brain tumor neoplasm classification and lesion localization in T1 contrast-enhanced axial MRI scans. Powered by a 100% from-scratch 4-stage convolutional neural network initialized via Kaiming (He) Normal variance, NEUROSCAN eliminates transfer learning shortcuts while resolving real-world clinical cohort imbalances (2.23:1) through a two-tier defense: WeightedRandomSampler mini-batch balancing and inverse class frequency cross-entropy loss weights. Gradient-Weighted Class Activation Mapping (Grad-CAM) provides transparent visual saliency overlays, validated on an untouched 10% test cohort achieving 100% sensitivity."
